2026-09-28 — K02h: full-width AArch64 logical-immediate selection and validation.

RED: the initial four-test MIR run has two passes and two failures: known
encodable masks still use register operands, and the validator accepts an
unencodable zero logical immediate. The initial selection repair then exposes
the separate C complement spelling (~4095UL): its XOR-with-all-ones result is
not retained as a constant fact. The first affected gate records 1075 PASS,
1 FAIL and 4 historical ignores. These are retained, not replaced by GREEN.

Implementation: AND/ORR/EOR on full bits<32>/bits<64> select the existing
immediate form only for a repeated power-of-two element with a nonempty,
nonfull cyclic run of ones. Either already-evaluated constant SSA operand may
be selected. Exact full-width constant bitwise expressions retain their facts;
their computations remain until normal dead-instruction removal. Zero,
all-ones, nonencoding masks, narrow/pair values and dynamic operands keep their
existing paths. Source evaluation, guards, tokens and volatile effects do not
change. MIR validation independently rejects malformed immediate operands.
This does not add an EqSat rule or a new instruction family.

The independent construction unit covers all 1302 W and 5334 X encodings,
plus 65536 deterministic random candidates per width and invalid high bits.
Five MIR integration tests cover 120 selected shapes, 600 exact EvoIR/MIR
value comparisons, 27 nonmatching controls, three dynamic controls, two
constant-expression chains and malformed-immediate rejection. The 120 shapes
assemble for Linux and Darwin (240 shape/target combinations). The CLI fixture
passes O0/O2 C-HIR, EvoIR, MIR and assembly assertions. All eleven targeted
logical/addend integration tests pass.

Sealed ARM64 native: fourteen controls pass, comprising six whole programs
(EvoCC/GCC14/Clang19 x O0/O2) and eight crossed caller/callee combinations.
Debug and optimized EvoCC produce byte-identical assembly for all six source
variants. The initial direct digest-name invocation failed image resolution
before executing any probe; native-image-resolution-error.log is retained.
Successful execution uses the installed sealed image with pre/post digest
verification and no guest network: 2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2.

Original KVM replay: the debug compiler times out on kvm_main at the unchanged
60-second limit. The explicitly optimized compiler then emits the two original
objects in 6.463 and 4.917 seconds. Both assemble and match all reference symbol
names/kinds. The actual outputs contain 938 and 307 logical-immediate
instructions respectively; these are current counts, not an attributed delta.
Original commands, configuration and installed objects remain unchanged.
No objects are installed and no kernel timing or boot PASS is inferred.
The active kernel build continues using frozen compiler 65035621f0921b11033455a2d02e72f94481fd6d3b82468279645a7a1e1fb3e5,
which does not include this repair. K02/K03 remain OPEN.

Affected five-crate gate against fd40569: 1077 PASS, zero failures, four
historical ignores; Clippy -D warnings and workspace fmt check PASS. The actual
host Rust/Clippy is 1.98.0 (88d9e12ae), not the build-environment contract's
1.97.1. This is a local affected-crate result, not the pinned final T05 gate.

